<p class="meta"><span class="kicker">GitHub tools for non-developers</span></p>
<h1>Free GitHub tools instead of paid ones, <span class="mark">installed and rated</span> by a non-developer</h1>
<p class="lead">I'm not a developer. I have AI install free tools from GitHub on my own computer, then write down how hard the install was, what broke, and the catch nobody mentions in the README. Every tool gets an install difficulty rating: ⭐ click only · ⭐⭐ follow the steps · ⭐⭐⭐ needs the terminal · 💀 gave up. If I haven't installed it, I don't rate it.</p>
<p class="golink"><a href="free/index.html">See a preview of free GitHub alternatives to monthly-subscription tools →</a></p>

